<h1><span lang="EN-GB">Properties</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="98.974%" size="6" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is accessible from the</span> <i style="font-style:normal;"><span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>tree context menu for entity or group &gt; Properties</b></span></i><span lang="EN-GB">.</span></p>
<p class="description"><span lang="EN-GB" class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span class="Command">Properties</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command calls the properties dialog for an entity or group. This dialog has two tabs – one that contains specific information (like number of points, stripes, triangles, normal, radius, etc.) for a particular type and the other called Common, which contains the extents and size of the entity/group. When call this command for an entity, the information from the dialog is copied in the</span> <u style="text-decoration:none;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="text-decoration:none;">Output pane</span></u><span lang="EN-GB">.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Following is a description of property dialogs for all data types in KUBE :</span></p>
<h2><span lang="EN-GB">Current CS</span></h2>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify; margin-left:19px;"><img src="properties_files/CurrentCS.gif" width="231px" height="17px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
<p class="sub-head"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Current CS entity</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">:</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>World CS</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">– orientation matrix of the current co-ordinate system.</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Common</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">– name and type of the currently active transformation, and its extents and size.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a22" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></span></p>
